eight is added up in that order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not overflow and is not NaN.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","